Upstream compiles tcg/perf.c and accepts -perfmap / -jitdump only on Linux
because Linux perf is the consumer; the map writer itself is plain stdio
(/tmp/perf-<pid>.map, one line per translated guest instruction: host pc,
size, guest-0x<pc>). tools/tcg-profile.py uses that map on macOS to
attribute `sample` hits in the code buffer to guest addresses.

